research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-separated-uniformizable-iff-tychonoff.md-168-
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-separated-uniformizable-iff-tychonoff.md-169-[L1] Uniformizable is equivalent to completely regular under dependent choice ([[thm-uniformizable-iff-completely-regular]]).
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-separated-uniformizable-iff-tychonoff.md-170-
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-separated-uniformizable-iff-tychonoff.md-171-[L2] A separated compatible uniformity induces a Hausdorff topology ([[thm-separated-uniformity-iff-induced-topology-is-hausdorff]]).
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-separated-uniformizable-iff-tychonoff.md-172-
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-separated-uniformizable-iff-tychonoff.md-173-[L3] Tychonoff means completely regular plus $T_1$ ([[def-completely-regular-and-tychonoff-spaces]], [[def-t0-and-t1-spaces]]).
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-separated-uniformizable-iff-tychonoff.md-174-
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-separated-uniformizable-iff-tychonoff.md:175:[L4] A completely regular topology is induced by the gauge $p_f(x,y)=|f(x)-f(y)|$ over all continuous $f:X\to[0,1]$ ([[lem-completely-regular-topologies-come-from-continuous-pseudometrics]], [[def-gauge-of-pseudometrics]]).
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-separated-uniformizable-iff-tychonoff.md-176-
research/audit/wave7-certifier-tasks/cor-separated-uniformizable-iff-tychonoff.md-177-[L5] Every Hausdorff space is $T_1$ ([[lem-urysohn-sits-between-hausdorff-and-regular-plus-t1]], clause 2).
