research/wave7-dispatch/orchestrator-A3-judgment.log-17087-**Proof technique:** direct.
research/wave7-dispatch/orchestrator-A3-judgment.log-17088-
research/wave7-dispatch/orchestrator-A3-judgment.log-17089-1.1 A separated-uniformizable space is completely regular by [L1] and Hausdorff by [L2], hence $T_1$ and therefore Tychonoff by [L3]. [L1, L2, L3]
research/wave7-dispatch/orchestrator-A3-judgment.log-17090-
research/wave7-dispatch/orchestrator-A3-judgment.log-17091-1.2 Conversely, let $X$ be Tychonoff. For $x\ne y$, the singleton $\{y\}$ is closed by $T_1$, and complete regularity gives a continuous $f:X\to[0,1]$ with $f(x)=1$ and $f(y)=0$. Thus the gauge in [L4] has an entourage excluding $(x,y)$, so its intersection is the diagonal and it is separated. It induces the original topology by [L4]. [L3, L4]
--
research/wave7-dispatch/orchestrator-A3-judgment.log-17246-
research/wave7-dispatch/orchestrator-A3-judgment.log-17247-1.1 Let $V$ be a target entourage and choose a symmetric $W$ with $W^{-1}\circ W=W^{\circ2}\subseteq V$. For each $x\in X$, the set $W[f(x)]$ is a neighbourhood of $f(x)$, so continuity gives an open neighbourhood $O_x$ of $x$ with $f[O_x]\subseteq W[f(x)]$. [L2, L3]
research/wave7-dispatch/orchestrator-A3-judgment.log-17248-
research/wave7-dispatch/orchestrator-A3-judgment.log-17249-2.1 The open cover $(O_x)_{x\in X}$ is uniform by [L3]. Hence there is a source entourage $E$ whose ball cover refines it: for each $a\in X$, some $O_x$ contains $E[a]$. [step 1.1, L1, L3]
research/wave7-dispatch/orchestrator-A3-judgment.log-17250-
research/wave7-dispatch/orchestrator-A3-judgment.log-17251-3.1 If $(a,b)\in E$, then $a,b\in E[a]\subseteq O_x$ for some $x$. Thus $f(a),f(b)\in W[f(x)]$, so $(f(a),f(b))\in W^{-1}\circ W\subseteq V$. This is uniform continuity. [step 1.1, step 2.1, L2] ∎
