research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-240800-+{"id":"thm-compact-hausdorff-space-has-a-unique-compatible-uniformity","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"Vienna Theorem 9.4.14 and Wodzicki Corollary 4.8 give uniqueness, with Vienna also giving existence, under the standard nonempty convention. The library admits empty compact Hausdorff space but no uniformity on it, so the exactly-one claim needs nonemptiness.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
