research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-264603-+{"id":"thm-topological-group-uniformities-induce-the-given-topology","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. BIU states the natural group uniformities induce the group topology in its Hausdorff uniformity section. The same proof works for arbitrary topological groups and inversion interchanges the two, but no located source states this exact non-Hausdorff package.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-264604-+{"id":"def-upper-and-roelcke-uniformities-of-a-topological-group","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf","https://homepages.math.uic.edu/~rosendal/PapersWebsite/Coarse-Geometry-Book23.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. BIU and Rosendal define the upper join and Roelcke meet with the displayed basic entourages for Hausdorff or Polish groups. The formulas extend unchanged to arbitrary topological groups, a standard convention, but the published domain is broader than the located sources.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-264605-+{"id":"cor-topological-groups-are-completely-regular","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Uniformizability of every topological group and complete regularity of uniformizable spaces are standard, but the item states their precise DC-dependent composition under the non-Hausdorff convention. No source states that exact package.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
