research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-300741-+{"id":"lem-uniformizable-spaces-are-regular","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources state the regularity consequence of a compatible uniformity with the same non-T1 convention. The proof is the standard entourage-shrinking argument.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-300742-+{"id":"lem-uniformizable-spaces-are-completely-regular","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf","https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Literature proves uniformizable spaces completely regular via pseudometrics, but the item makes DC explicit as the construction principle. No source with that same foundational hypothesis surfaced.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log:300743:+{"id":"lem-completely-regular-topologies-come-from-continuous-pseudometrics","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf","https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"Vienna Theorem 9.4.15 and BIU use continuous functions p_f(x,y)=|f(x)-f(y)| to recover the topology. The item makes the gauge explicit; its empty-carrier and triangle-inequality citation defects are escalated.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-300744-+{"id":"thm-uniformizable-iff-completely-regular","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf","https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. The uniformization theorem is standard, but the biconditional asserts DC suffices and the local definition admits empty completely regular space while proper filters exclude it. No source matches both conventions and hypothesis.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-300745-+{"id":"cor-separated-uniformizable-iff-tychonoff","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf","https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. The separated uniformization theorem is standard, but the item exposes DC and the library Tychonoff convention. Empty carrier is currently a counterexample, and T1/Hausdorff bridge citations are incomplete.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-300746-+{"id":"def-topological-group","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"The BIU notes define a topological group by continuity of multiplication and inversion, exactly matching the item.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-300747-+{"id":"lem-topological-group-translations-and-inversion","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"The BIU notes state that left and right shifts and inversion are homeomorphisms. The proof expands continuity and inverse formulas.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-300748-+{"id":"def-left-and-right-uniformities-of-a-topological-group","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. BIU gives exactly these entourage formulas under an explicit Hausdorff hypothesis, while the item correctly defines them for arbitrary, possibly non-Hausdorff topological groups. Dropping Hausdorff is standard established mathematics, but it is a genuine hypothesis delta and no matching source surfaced.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-300749-+{"id":"thm-topological-group-uniformities-induce-the-given-topology","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. BIU states the natural group uniformities induce the group topology in its Hausdorff uniformity section. The same proof works for arbitrary topological groups and inversion interchanges the two, but no located source states this exact non-Hausdorff package.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-300750-+{"id":"def-upper-and-roelcke-uniformities-of-a-topological-group","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf","https://homepages.math.uic.edu/~rosendal/PapersWebsite/Coarse-Geometry-Book23.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. BIU and Rosendal define the upper join and Roelcke meet with the displayed basic entourages for Hausdorff or Polish groups. The formulas extend unchanged to arbitrary topological groups, a standard convention, but the published domain is broader than the located sources.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-300751-+{"id":"cor-topological-groups-are-completely-regular","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Uniformizability of every topological group and complete regularity of uniformizable spaces are standard, but the item states their precise DC-dependent composition under the non-Hausdorff convention. No source states that exact package.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
