research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-345026-+{"id":"lem-countable-uniform-base-normalisation","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Decreasing symmetric bases with triple-composite control are the standard metrization normalization, but the item emphasizes its finite-intersection recursion works in ZF. No located source states this exact choice-free proposition.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-345027-+{"id":"thm-countably-based-uniformity-is-pseudometrizable","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf","https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources give pseudometrizability of countably based uniformities and the separated criterion for the pseudometric to distinguish points. The item packages both; its metric criterion needs a direct metric-definition citation.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-345028-+{"id":"def-uniformizable-space","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"Wodzicki and Vienna define uniformizable as having a compatible uniformity; the item additionally names the standard separated variant without altering either definition.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-345029-+{"id":"lem-uniformizable-spaces-are-regular","statement":"literature-derived","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"exact-source","urls":["https://math.berkeley.edu/~wodzicki/H104.F13/UniformStructure-alt.pdf","https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources state the regularity consequence of a compatible uniformity with the same non-T1 convention. The proof is the standard entourage-shrinking argument.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-345030-+{"id":"lem-uniformizable-spaces-are-completely-regular","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf","https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. Literature proves uniformizable spaces completely regular via pseudometrics, but the item makes DC explicit as the construction principle. No source with that same foundational hypothesis surfaced.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log:345031:+{"id":"lem-completely-regular-topologies-come-from-continuous-pseudometrics","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf","https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"Vienna Theorem 9.4.15 and BIU use continuous functions p_f(x,y)=|f(x)-f(y)| to recover the topology. The item makes the gauge explicit; its empty-carrier and triangle-inequality citation defects are escalated.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-345032-+{"id":"thm-uniformizable-iff-completely-regular","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf","https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. The uniformization theorem is standard, but the biconditional asserts DC suffices and the local definition admits empty completely regular space while proper filters exclude it. No source matches both conventions and hypothesis.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
research/audit/wave7-dispatch/audit-beta-topology-uniform.log-345033-+{"id":"cor-separated-uniformizable-iff-tychonoff","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"established-knowledge","urls":["https://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~mike/teaching/ss16/general_topology.pdf","https://u.math.biu.ac.il/~megereli/TGrNotes070217.pdf"],"rationale":"ESCALATED TO ALPHA. The separated uniformization theorem is standard, but the item exposes DC and the library Tychonoff convention. Empty carrier is currently a counterexample, and T1/Hausdorff bridge citations are incomplete.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-08"}
